In Lightroom one filename-template editor serves import, Rename Photos and Export, so a scheme like `{date}_{title}_{seq}` works the same everywhere. LightCraft already had that template language for Rename Photos and import renaming (`rename::expand`: `{seq:N}`, `{date:%…}`, `{camera}`, `{title}`, `{ext}`). Export had its own three-token version: `{name}`, `{seq}` and `{date}` (YYYYMMDD only). So `Trip-{seq:2}` or `{date:%Y-%m-%d}_{title}` worked when renaming but came out literally in exported file names.

### What changed
- `rename::expand_tokens(template, photo, seq, seq_width)`: the token expansion of `rename::expand`, without the sanitizing and extension handling, so callers can do those their own way. `expand` (rename + import) uses it unchanged.
- Export (`ExportOptions::file_name_for(photo, seq)`) now uses it, so every rename token works in exports. Export-specific behaviour is kept:
  - a bare `{seq}` still pads to 3 digits;
  - `start_number` still applies;
  - path separators still become `_`;
  - `Original` exports still keep the original extension.
  If every token comes out empty (e.g. `{title}` on an untitled photo), the original name is used instead of a hidden `.jpg`.
- New tokens, shared by rename, import and export (Lightroom has these too):
  - `{num}`: the number at the end of the file name (`DSC_0815` → `0815`; Lightroom's "Filename number suffix");
  - `{folder}`: the original's folder name;
  - `{lens}`, `{iso}`, `{rating}`, `{creator}`.
- `{date}` in exports now falls back to the import date when there's no capture time, as rename does, instead of expanding to nothing.
- Export dialog: the field hint mentions the new tokens, and the start number also shows for `{seq:N}`. The Rename dialog's token list is updated, and so are the command docs and `parity.md` (LR-EXP-NAMING, LR-LIB-RENAME) and `whats-new.md`.
- MCP `export` tool: its parameter whitelist now passes `startNumber` (it was dropped before), and the `naming` description lists the to…

## Summary

Apple ProRAW now renders like Lightroom Classic 15.6, and XMP presets applied to it do too. Every model is fitted to Lightroom's own exports of the CC0 iPhone 12 Pro ProRAW in the corpus (`dng-apple-iphone12pro-proraw.dng`, raw.pixls.us). The reference renders stay in the gitignored `plan/`: one per slider, per slider pair and per preset group, at 2000 px and at full size, plus a synthetic chart carrying the file's own colour tags.

Mean CIEDE2000 against Lightroom's 2000 px exports of the same file:

| | Before | After |
|---|---:|---:|
| Unedited ProRAW | 19.5 | **0.58** |
| Real XMP preset A | 18.9 | **0.70** |
| Real XMP preset B | 22.7 | **0.87** |
| Real XMP preset C | 22.7 | **2.12** |

```text
raw / DNG   JPEG XL DNG tiles (DNG 1.7); DNG semantic mattes → Sky / Subject / People masks;
            ProRAW gain table map kept, not rendered (as Lightroom); ProfileToneCurve per channel;
            a preset's LensProfileEnable=0 keeps embedded lens corrections
tone        Lightroom's base operator (per BaselineExposure + Exposure, generated lr_tables.rs);
            Highlights / Shadows → Whites → Blacks → profile curve → Contrast (order measured from slider pairs);
            Contrast keys on the 33rd percentile of log luminance
colour      WB re-evaluates the camera matrices at the new white (Lightroom's tint sign);
            calibration = linear-ProPhoto matrix + subtractive shadows tint; Lightroom's HSL mixer;
            Vibrance / Saturation and grading fitted, grading after the curves;
            natural cubic point curves; parametric regions in sequence; curves in a fixed curve space
detail      sharpening = Lightroom's law on the finished image (Amount / Radius / Detail / Masking at full size),
            CPU + GPU (two passes of the per-pixel kernel); colour NR refitted; ProRAW imports at Sharpening 50 / Radius 1.4
export      smaller than the photo → rendered at full size, downsized Catmull-Rom on gamma-1.8 values (as Lightroom)
```

