## Problem

The app has no reduced-motion option, and it ignores the system's Reduce Motion setting. Everything that moves always moves:
- the 0.22 s click-zoom (a click on the photo, or Z);
- egui's built-in widget easing (`animation_time` 0.08 s);
- the glide when the grid or filmstrip scrolls to the active photo;
- the Synchronize Folder spinner;
- the activity bar's sweep while it doesn't know how much work there is.

The only thing a person could turn off was the slideshow fade. People with vestibular disorders, and anyone who has asked their system for less motion, get it anyway (WCAG 2.3.3, Animation from Interactions). The code says so itself: "There is no reduced-motion setting in the app".

## Change

- **The setting:** Settings ▸ Interface ▸ **Reduce motion**.
  - **Default:** it follows macOS's Reduce Motion (System Settings ▸ Accessibility ▸ Display) until you tick or untick it. Then your choice wins, and **Use the system setting** beside it hands the choice back.
  - **Elsewhere:** Windows, Linux and the web have no system value here, so it is off until you turn it on.
  - **Command:** `view.reduceMotion` (`{on?}`, or `{follow: true}`), with no params toggling. It replies `{on, followsSystem}`.
- **One policy place:** `crates/ui-egui/src/motion.rs`. Every animation asks it, and its module doc states the rule: with Reduce motion on, things that move or turn stop moving, while opacity fades that tell a state change stay.
- **With it on:**
  - a click on the photo or Z zooms at once;
  - egui's widget easing stops (`animation_time` 0);
  - scrolling to a photo jumps instead of gliding (`scroll_animation` none);
  - the Synchronize Folder spinner is a still dot of the same size;
  - the activity bar shows a still segment;
  - a theme change keeps all of this.
- **Unchanged:** toast fades and the slideshow's crossfade and control bar fade. Pinch and scroll zoom were never animated.
